   "source": [
    "# 02_wgan_gp : WGAN-GP (PyTorch) — implémentation et explications en français\n",
    "\n",
    "Objectifs :\n",
    "- Comprendre la différence WGAN vs GAN classique.\n",
    "- Implémenter le critic (discriminateur), la pénalité sur le gradient (GP) et la boucle d'entraînement WGAN-GP.\n",
    "- Tester sur le même dataset Pareto / pertes et comparer les quantiles extrêmes.\n",
    "\n",
    "Ce notebook est commenté pas-à-pas pour un débutant."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Rappel conceptuel rapide\n",
    "\n",
    "- WGAN repose sur la distance de Wasserstein (Earth-Mover) entre distributions, qui a des gradients plus utiles quand les distributions ne se superposent pas.\n",
    "- Pour appliquer WGAN, il faut contraindre le critic à être 1-Lipschitz. WGAN-GP (gradient penalty) est une méthode populaire pour imposer cette contrainte en pénalisant la norme du gradient du critic par rapport à ses entrées.\n",
    "\n",
    "Formule de la penalty : lambda * E[(||grad(D(interpolated))||2 - 1)^2]\n",
    "où interpolated est un mélange entre vraies et fausses données."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "import torch.optim as optim\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, TensorDataset\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from tqdm import tqdm\n",
    "\n",
    "device = torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')\n",
    "print('Device:', device)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Définitions : critic, generator et gradient penalty\n",
    "\n",
    "On réutilise une architecture MLP simple adaptée pour WGAN (pas de Sigmoid sur le critic).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class Generator(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, z_dim=16, hidden_dim=128):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.net = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Linear(z_dim, hidden_dim),\n",
    "            nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.Linear(hidden_dim, hidden_dim),\n",
    "            nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.Linear(hidden_dim, 1),\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    def forward(self, z):\n",
    "        return self.net(z).squeeze(-1)\n",
    "\n",
    "class Critic(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, hidden_dim=128):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.net = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Linear(1, hidden_dim),\n",
    "            nn.LeakyReLU(0.2),\n",
    "            nn.Linear(hidden_dim, hidden_dim),\n",
    "            nn.LeakyReLU(0.2),\n",
    "            nn.Linear(hidden_dim, 1),\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    def forward(self, x):\n",
    "        x = x.unsqueeze(-1).float()\n",
    "        return self.net(x).squeeze(-1)\n",
    "\n",
    "def gradient_penalty(critic, real, fake, device='cpu', lambda_gp=10.0):\n",
    "    # Interpoler entre réel et fake\n",
    "    batch_size = real.size(0)\n",
    "    eps = torch.rand(batch_size, 1, device=device)\n",
    "    eps = eps.expand_as(real)\n",
    "    interpolated = eps * real + (1 - eps) * fake\n",
    "    interpolated.requires_grad_(True)\n",
    "    # Calculer critic(interpolated)\n",
    "    prob_interpolated = critic(interpolated)\n",
    "    # Gradient de la sortie par rapport à interpolated\n",
    "    gradients = torch.autograd.grad(outputs=prob_interpolated, inputs=interpolated,\n",
    "                                     grad_outputs=torch.ones_like(prob_interpolated),\n",
    "                                     create_graph=True, retain_graph=True)[0]\n",
    "    gradients = gradients.view(batch_size, -1)\n",
    "    grad_norm = gradients.norm(2, dim=1)\n",
    "    gp = ((grad_norm - 1) ** 2).mean() * lambda_gp\n",
    "    return gp\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Boucle d'entraînement WGAN-GP (explications)\n",
    "\n",
    "- On entraîne le critic plusieurs fois par itération (n_critic) puis le générateur une fois.\n",
    "- Loss critic : E[D(fake)] - E[D(real)] + GP\n",
    "- Loss generator : -E[D(fake)] (on cherche à maximiser la valeur que le critic attribue aux faux échantillons).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Fonction d'entraînement WGAN-GP sur données 1D (log-échelle ou autre)\n",
    "def train_wgan_gp(data_array, z_dim=16, n_epochs=200, batch_size=128, lr=1e-4, n_critic=5, lambda_gp=10.0, device=None):\n",
    "    if device is None:\n",
    "        device = torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')\n",
    "    X = torch.tensor(data_array, dtype=torch.float32).unsqueeze(-1)\n",
    "    loader = DataLoader(TensorDataset(X), batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "    G = Generator(z_dim=z_dim).to(device)\n",
    "    C = Critic().to(device)\n",
    "    opt_G = optim.Adam(G.parameters(), lr=lr, betas=(0.5, 0.9))\n",
    "    opt_C = optim.Adam(C.parameters(), lr=lr, betas=(0.5, 0.9))\n",
    "\n",
    "    history = {'c_loss': [], 'g_loss': []}\n",
    "    for epoch in range(n_epochs):\n",
    "        c_losses = []\n",
    "        g_losses = []\n",
    "        for i, batch in enumerate(loader):\n",
    "            real = batch[0].to(device)\n",
    "            bs = real.size(0)\n",
    "            # entraîner critic n_critic fois\n",
    "            for _ in range(n_critic):\n",
    "                z = torch.randn(bs, z_dim, device=device)\n",
    "                fake = G(z).unsqueeze(-1)\n",
    "                # critic outputs scalar (no sigmoid)\n",
    "                C.zero_grad()\n",
    "                loss_critic = (C(fake) - C(real)).mean()\n",
    "                gp = gradient_penalty(C, real, fake, device=device, lambda_gp=lambda_gp)\n",
    "                loss_C_total = loss_critic + gp\n",
    "                loss_C_total.backward()\n",
    "                opt_C.step()\n",
    "            # === entraîner G une fois ===\n",
    "            G.zero_grad()\n",
    "            z = torch.randn(bs, z_dim, device=device)\n",
    "            gen = G(z).unsqueeze(-1)\n",
    "            loss_G = -C(gen).mean()\n",
    "            loss_G.backward()\n",
    "            opt_G.step()\n",
    "\n",
    "            c_losses.append(loss_C_total.item())\n",
    "            g_losses.append(loss_G.item())\n",
    "\n",
    "        history['c_loss'].append(np.mean(c_losses))\n",
    "        history['g_loss'].append(np.mean(g_losses))\n",
    "        if (epoch+1) % 20 == 0:\n",
    "            print(f'Epoch {epoch+1}/{n_epochs}  C_loss={history["c_loss"][-1]:.4f}  G_loss={history["g_loss"][-1]:.4f}')\n",
    "    return G, C, history\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Test rapide sur une loi de Pareto (comme dans le notebook 01)\n",
    "\n",
    "On utilise les mêmes données simulées et on compare les quantiles p99/p99.9 entre réel et généré."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Générer données Pareto (log)\n",
    "def sample_pareto(size, xm=1.0, alpha=2.0, seed=None):\n",
    "    if seed is not None:\n",
    "        np.random.seed(seed)\n",
    "    u = np.random.rand(size)\n",
    "    return xm / (u ** (1.0 / alpha))\n",
    "\n",
    "n = 15000\n",
    "data = sample_pareto(n, xm=1.0, alpha=2.0)\n",
    "data_log = np.log(data)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Entraîner WGAN-GP (peut prendre du temps selon GPU)\n",
    "G_w, C_w, history_w = train_wgan_gp(data_log, z_dim=16, n_epochs=120, batch_size=128, lr=1e-4, n_critic=5, lambda_gp=10.0, device=device)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Générer échantillons\n",
    "G_w.eval()\n",
    "with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "    z = torch.randn(20000, 16, device=device)\n",
    "    gen_samples = G_w(z).cpu().numpy()\n",
    "gen_exp = np.exp(gen_samples)\n",
    "real_exp = np.exp(data_log)\n",
    "\n",
    "for q in [0.95, 0.99, 0.999]:\n",
    "    rq = np.quantile(real_exp, q)\n",
    "    gq = np.quantile(gen_exp, q)\n",
    "    print(f'q={q:.3f}  réel={rq:.4f}  généré={gq:.4f}  ratio={gq/rq:.3f}')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
